<title>USA: O.I. increases share buyback program.</title>
<headline>O.I. increases share buyback program.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGE STATION, Texas 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>O.I. Corp said on Thursday its board authorized the repurchase of up to a further 400,000 shares of common stock, boosting a previous buyback authorization.</p>
<p>In December, the company said its board had authorized the repurchase of 400,000 shares.</p>
<p>Purchases would be made from time to time in the open market, or via private transactions at prices the company considered attractive, O.I. said.</p>
<p>Repurchased shares would replace stock issued in acquisitions, the company said.</p>
<p>O.I. develops, makes and markets instruments used to prepare, detect, measure, analyze and monitor chemical compounds.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
